# An extension's chip, peek and epeek (src/chips/dialog_test.zig): styled
# text, both dots, buttons, the filter and its help list, hover events,
# and opening by itself without the keyboard. Run from a window 1100 wide
# with four standard chips (the extension's chip about x 470, y 618):
#   gtty --script test/peek.gt
# Expected: pk1 a bold + yellow chip; pk2 a peek, its "line" struck through,
# ⋯ and ×; status "said: … data=chip". pk3 status data=horizontal. pk4 the
# list: add / hosts / save, ⋮ on beta, ⋯ on gamma, save on delta. pk5
# "alpha" and "alpine" offered, the list's "al" marked. pk6 Tab: "alpha".
# pk7 the popup Rename / Delete. pk8 status id=delete. pk9 status
# id=epsilon (a hover). pk10 the list open, the filter box dim, the prompt
# label says #1. pk11 closed, "x" typed in the shell.
/s zsh
/wait 1500
/dialog peek
/wait 400
/shot pk1-chip.bmp
/click 470 618
/wait 400
/shot pk2-peek.bmp
/click 544 612
/wait 300
/shot pk3-dots.bmp
/click 436 612
/wait 500
/shot pk4-epeek.bmp
/text al
/wait 400
/shot pk5-filter.bmp
/key tab
/wait 300
/shot pk6-tab.bmp
/key backspace
/key backspace
/key backspace
/key backspace
/key backspace
/wait 300
/click 641 433
/wait 400
/shot pk7-menu.bmp
/key down
/key down
/key enter
/wait 300
/shot pk8-picked.bmp
/move 470 500
/wait 800
/shot pk9-hover.bmp
/key escape
/wait 300
/dialog peekOpen
/wait 400
/shot pk10-unasked.bmp
/text x
/wait 300
/dialog peekClose
/wait 400
/shot pk11-closed.bmp
/quit
